00:56:50.650 --> 00:56:53.550
Some international
community might think that

00:56:53.550 --> 00:56:58.183
the way democracy movement
in Myanmar is only violent.

00:57:03.648 --> 00:57:05.460
(indistinct) Violence.

00:57:05.460 --> 00:57:09.130
They feel that these two ways
could be more effective to...

00:57:10.540 --> 00:57:12.420
But, that could be true.

00:57:12.420 --> 00:57:14.960
But on the other hand what
we have to think is that

00:57:14.960 --> 00:57:16.630
the suffering of the...

00:57:18.918 --> 00:57:20.310
The civilians, people,

00:57:20.310 --> 00:57:22.090
those who do not join in this armed group.

00:57:22.090 --> 00:57:25.070
Like for example, now
in Mindat, my hometown,

00:57:25.070 --> 00:57:26.137
and then (indistinct).

00:57:27.910 --> 00:57:30.400
Because of this violent fight

00:57:30.400 --> 00:57:32.700
many civilians left their hometown.

00:57:32.700 --> 00:57:35.140
Like for example, Thantlang in Chin state,

00:57:35.140 --> 00:57:39.010
only 28 people stayed in their town.

00:57:39.010 --> 00:57:42.050
And the rest of the people
they just fled to jungles,

00:57:42.050 --> 00:57:43.710
and some of them (indistinct).

00:57:43.710 --> 00:57:46.240
And so what I can say here is that,

00:57:46.240 --> 00:57:49.040
violence could be a good way
to defeat this dictatorship,

00:57:49.040 --> 00:57:51.120
but we also need to consider the suffering

00:57:51.120 --> 00:57:54.900
of those innocent people.

00:57:54.900 --> 00:57:56.340
In that case, I really don't know how the

00:57:56.340 --> 00:57:59.980
international community could
do some help more effectively.

00:57:59.980 --> 00:58:01.383
That might be my additions.

