might be put on to the Junta?

00:59:27.700 --> 00:59:30.850
Maybe Scot, I'll ask you
to start that conversation,

00:59:30.850 --> 00:59:33.150
but again, not leave it
all on your shoulders.

00:59:35.030 --> 00:59:36.963
- Thanks, I appreciate that Erik.

00:59:38.470 --> 00:59:40.500
Again, I certainly can't speak

00:59:40.500 --> 00:59:42.843
for the US government on this.

00:59:43.953 --> 00:59:47.583
(indistinct) On attending
the ASEAN meetings.

00:59:48.852 --> 00:59:52.290
But I can say in previous discussions,

00:59:52.290 --> 00:59:55.830
internal US governments
discussions that I was a part of,

00:59:55.830 --> 00:59:58.660
some years ago on sanctions.

00:59:58.660 --> 01:00:02.090
The approach generally was to look at

01:00:02.090 --> 01:00:03.630
what's the impact of the sanctions.

01:00:03.630 --> 01:00:06.280
In this case the goal is clear,

01:00:06.280 --> 01:00:09.240
which is to squeeze the Junta's finances.

01:00:09.240 --> 01:00:11.060
The Biden administration
has made that clear

01:00:11.060 --> 01:00:13.760
through the actions it's already taken.

01:00:13.760 --> 01:00:15.300
The other side of that is

01:00:15.300 --> 01:00:20.300
what are the negative
consequences of any sanctions.

01:00:20.470 --> 01:00:22.110
And so, in some cases

01:00:22.110 --> 01:00:23.990
if you got a really broad sanctions,

01:00:23.990 --> 01:00:27.060
you could be harming
a lot of other people.

01:00:27.060 --> 01:00:29.480
I would guess in the context of looking at

01:00:29.480 --> 01:00:31.070
potential Motegi sanctions, again,

01:00:31.070 --> 01:00:33.770
it's a what are the positives,

01:00:33.770 --> 01:00:37.350
ie reducing revenue to
the regime, to the Junta.

01:00:37.350 --> 01:00:41.280
Versus whatever costs or
downsides there are of that,

01:00:41.280 --> 01:00:44.770
and I'm not privy to those
conversations so I don't know

01:00:45.950 --> 01:00:47.350
how that's going.

01:00:47.350 --> 01:00:49.920
In terms of the president's
potential participation

01:00:49.920 --> 01:00:51.000
in the ASEAN meetings.

01:00:51.000 --> 01:00:52.740
I think it's really important.

01:00:52.740 --> 01:00:54.700
I don't know what the
White House is thinking,

01:00:54.700 --> 01:00:56.500
or what it will do, of course.

01:00:56.500 --> 01:00:57.400
I think it's important,

01:00:57.400 --> 01:00:59.700
this is not just a Myanmar issue,

01:00:59.700 --> 01:01:01.970
this is all of Southeast Asia.

01:01:01.970 --> 01:01:04.250
Ten countries, 600 million people,

01:01:04.250 --> 01:01:07.450
so the president's
participation in those meetings

01:01:07.450 --> 01:01:09.330
is really important.

01:01:09.330 --> 01:01:14.330
Because of an entire region
that's quite in many ways.

01:01:15.500 --> 01:01:19.810
And where I think there's
a strong demand for,

01:01:19.810 --> 01:01:23.280
in the region, for the US participation.

01:01:23.280 --> 01:01:27.190
Obviously it wouldn't be
any president's first choice

01:01:27.190 --> 01:01:29.747
to sit down at a meeting
that includes (indistinct).

01:01:33.759 --> 01:01:36.480
If the president does
decide to participate,

01:01:36.480 --> 01:01:38.827
I think it's important
not to take that as,

01:01:38.827 --> 01:01:40.310
"Oh, he's okay with the Junta."

01:01:40.310 --> 01:01:42.310
Clearly we're not, the United States

01:01:42.310 --> 01:01:43.980
is not okay with the Junta.

01:01:43.980 --> 01:01:45.260
But it is important to look at it

01:01:45.260 --> 01:01:47.380
in the context of the overall relationship

01:01:47.380 --> 01:01:49.210
with all of Southeast Asia,

01:01:49.210 --> 01:01:51.193
not just in the Myanmar context.

01:01:57.580 --> 01:02:00.180
- I'd be interested to hear
from the other panelists

01:02:01.300 --> 01:02:05.080
about the symbolic meaning of if Biden

01:02:05.080 --> 01:02:06.620
were to sit down at the table.

01:02:06.620 --> 01:02:09.550
How would that be received among...

01:02:10.920 --> 01:02:13.000
People in Myanmar,

01:02:13.000 --> 01:02:18.000
members of the NUG and
other affiliated groups

01:02:18.050 --> 01:02:20.920
interested in the Myanmar
situation right now,

01:02:20.920 --> 01:02:22.270
out of curiosity.

01:02:22.270 --> 01:02:24.243
Maybe we could start with Ma Thida.

01:02:25.660 --> 01:02:28.740
- Well, I think the, first of all,

01:02:28.740 --> 01:02:30.680
I think the international community

01:02:30.680 --> 01:02:34.023
should accept the failure
of the five-point consensus.

01:02:35.460 --> 01:02:37.620
Regarding the ASEAN intervention.

01:02:37.620 --> 01:02:41.080
I think they did, if we
cannot recognize this,

01:02:41.080 --> 01:02:45.330
we will end up at the (indistinct)
of ASEAN all the time.

01:02:45.330 --> 01:02:47.486
Even though we are the part of ASEAN,

01:02:47.486 --> 01:02:49.760
ASEAN, every single country said that

01:02:49.760 --> 01:02:52.333
ASEAN cannot guarantee any democracy,

01:02:52.333 --> 01:02:55.150
because they are still
struggling by themselves.

01:02:55.150 --> 01:02:58.120
So for that reason I think even though

01:02:58.120 --> 01:03:02.420
the US intervention is just...

01:03:02.420 --> 01:03:05.120
Through the platform of the UN,

01:03:05.120 --> 01:03:10.120
or by itself to encourage
more intervention.

01:03:10.150 --> 01:03:12.870
True ASEANs will not work.

01:03:12.870 --> 01:03:16.410
But at the same time, I think the...

01:03:19.210 --> 01:03:21.700
I hope, I seriously do hope,

01:03:21.700 --> 01:03:25.080
but it's not very promising.

01:03:25.080 --> 01:03:27.443
The current, the UN assembly,

01:03:28.830 --> 01:03:31.460
people, the other countries, should also

01:03:31.460 --> 01:03:35.270
seriously think about their
role for the intervention,

01:03:35.270 --> 01:03:36.530
not just US.

01:03:36.530 --> 01:03:39.340
Because somehow, for example...

01:03:40.400 --> 01:03:45.390
We still do need to take
account for the intervention

01:03:45.390 --> 01:03:48.230
from the China and Russia.

01:03:48.230 --> 01:03:51.580
Because the people-to-people relationship

01:03:52.530 --> 01:03:56.600
among the Myanmar and
China is very, very...

01:03:58.000 --> 01:03:58.930
Obvious.

01:03:58.930 --> 01:04:03.750
My concern is they are a cover
of a diplomatic relationship,

01:04:03.750 --> 01:04:07.120
it's sometimes it's purely the GDG.

01:04:07.120 --> 01:04:10.080
And this kind of things
cannot work properly,

01:04:10.080 --> 01:04:12.920
because the GDG pressure will

01:04:13.770 --> 01:04:16.267
only affect on the SAC,

01:04:16.267 --> 01:04:17.232
the Tatmadaw.

01:04:17.232 --> 01:04:20.250
Because it's turned out to be
like the current government.

01:04:20.250 --> 01:04:23.690
But what we do need is more intervention

01:04:23.690 --> 01:04:26.573
through the other platform,
P to P, people to people.

01:04:26.573 --> 01:04:28.840
Through the civil society organizations,

01:04:28.840 --> 01:04:31.910
through the academy
institution, so and so.

01:04:31.910 --> 01:04:36.580
So in that case, ASEAN is
also another big challenge,

01:04:36.580 --> 01:04:39.220
because the most of the ASEAN countries

01:04:39.220 --> 01:04:42.560
turn out to be the refuge area

01:04:42.560 --> 01:04:46.070
for the military families members too.

01:04:46.070 --> 01:04:49.911
So in that case, I think the...

01:04:49.911 --> 01:04:54.430
The pressure from the other
countries, including US,

01:04:54.430 --> 01:04:58.080
towards the ASEAN countries is not to

01:04:58.080 --> 01:05:00.980
become part of the refuge.

01:05:00.980 --> 01:05:03.340
Police for the military officers

01:05:03.340 --> 01:05:06.810
in terms of the legal immigration status.

01:05:06.810 --> 01:05:11.390
Or the other other way,
economic investment,

01:05:11.390 --> 01:05:12.710
something like that.

01:05:12.710 --> 01:05:16.740
We should think about some
other ways to make the...

01:05:18.890 --> 01:05:20.740
Pressure on the ASEAN itself.

01:05:20.740 --> 01:05:23.430
So, first of all, we need
to acknowledge the failure

01:05:23.430 --> 01:05:24.760
of the five-point consensus.

01:05:24.760 --> 01:05:26.800
It's already gone from my eyes.

01:05:26.800 --> 01:05:30.540
So we should think about a new strategy,

01:05:30.540 --> 01:05:35.290
and the solution, not
just through only ASEAN.

01:05:35.290 --> 01:05:38.530
Then we should build up the

01:05:38.530 --> 01:05:40.210
more

01:05:40.210 --> 01:05:45.000
cooperative and collective
solutions through more countries,

01:05:45.000 --> 01:05:46.213
not just ASEAN.

01:05:47.880 --> 01:05:48.984
- Thank you.

01:05:48.984 --> 01:05:50.873
Tun, did you want to add to this?

01:05:52.150 --> 01:05:55.240
- I could if I...

01:05:55.240 --> 01:05:56.330
Unlock.

01:05:56.330 --> 01:05:57.970
I think the...

01:06:00.530 --> 01:06:01.950
What Ma Thida said is a very eloquent

01:06:01.950 --> 01:06:05.740
in terms of how useful ASEAN
would be for the United States.

01:06:05.740 --> 01:06:10.190
If Biden administration want
to create another platform,

01:06:10.190 --> 01:06:12.230
we need to really reconsider,

01:06:12.230 --> 01:06:14.900
not based on that five-point
diplomatic attempt,

01:06:14.900 --> 01:06:16.380
it started out.

01:06:16.380 --> 01:06:18.440
But it has to be a different format.

01:06:18.440 --> 01:06:21.370
But from the point of view
of the people inside Burma,

01:06:21.370 --> 01:06:23.570
CDM participant, the protestor themselves,

01:06:23.570 --> 01:06:25.040
and the citizen themselves.

01:06:25.040 --> 01:06:27.640
They have no really big hope

01:06:27.640 --> 01:06:30.150
in times of international intervention.

01:06:30.150 --> 01:06:31.160
They understand it.

01:06:31.160 --> 01:06:32.083
But the only thing that they want is the

01:06:32.083 --> 01:06:35.620
international community support
national unity government,

01:06:35.620 --> 01:06:38.220
which is the elected government of Burma.

01:06:38.220 --> 01:06:42.360
November 8th, 2020 elected
government of Burma or Myanmar.

01:06:42.360 --> 01:06:45.800
And that government should be,
for international community,

01:06:45.800 --> 01:06:47.380
easy to support.

01:06:47.380 --> 01:06:50.140
The UN is now under way with the UNGA.

01:06:51.660 --> 01:06:53.430
It is recently just yesterday,

01:06:53.430 --> 01:06:58.170
it's a schedule that
(indistinct) about to speak.

01:06:58.170 --> 01:07:02.860
Give a speech on September
27th was set aside

01:07:02.860 --> 01:07:06.690
because the credit share
committee is dealing with

01:07:06.690 --> 01:07:09.620
sensitive political
issue within (indistinct)

01:07:09.620 --> 01:07:10.723
on the Burma question.

01:07:11.580 --> 01:07:13.650
It is really a shame for the UN

01:07:13.650 --> 01:07:15.557
not to be able to bravely support

01:07:15.557 --> 01:07:17.823
the elected government of Burma.

01:07:20.400 --> 01:07:22.090
The United Nations security council

01:07:22.090 --> 01:07:24.160
should at least now begin to table

01:07:24.160 --> 01:07:27.460
substantive discussion and
maybe have taken action

01:07:27.460 --> 01:07:31.240
on the economic and (indistinct) goal.

01:07:31.240 --> 01:07:34.500
Especially (indistinct) goal,
against the military regime.

01:07:34.500 --> 01:07:36.720
So these framework could be discussed.

01:07:36.720 --> 01:07:41.440
If Biden want to create a
new framework with ASEAN,

01:07:41.440 --> 01:07:43.990
that's the first thing that
United States have to state

01:07:43.990 --> 01:07:44.890
is a baseline.

01:07:44.890 --> 01:07:48.543
The baseline is as ambassador
Marciel have already indicated

01:07:48.543 --> 01:07:51.360
that current military
leadership made outline,

01:07:51.360 --> 01:07:55.460
and the top SAC member
has to be set aside.

01:07:55.460 --> 01:07:56.910
They need to step out of it,

01:07:56.910 --> 01:07:58.770
a new generation of military leader.

01:07:58.770 --> 01:08:01.950
If Biden want to sort of
create that framework,

01:08:01.950 --> 01:08:04.290
if ASEAN want to create that framework.

01:08:04.290 --> 01:08:07.410
But it is really for the Myanmar public,

01:08:07.410 --> 01:08:10.230
it is impossible to
accept even to that level.

01:08:10.230 --> 01:08:12.240
Due to what Ma Thida has eloquently stated

01:08:12.240 --> 01:08:15.700
about the level of trust
to this institution.

01:08:15.700 --> 01:08:17.670
I think we are dealing with

01:08:17.670 --> 01:08:20.100
the traditionally state centric politic

01:08:20.100 --> 01:08:22.170
that the world is used to.

01:08:22.170 --> 01:08:25.860
And here a very important politic

01:08:25.860 --> 01:08:29.250
that is defined by the public in Burma.

01:08:29.250 --> 01:08:30.910
Never been before in the world,

01:08:30.910 --> 01:08:34.100
that we are seeing such
a scale of resilient,

01:08:34.100 --> 01:08:38.550
robust population that is
against their own state.

01:08:38.550 --> 01:08:41.010
And so this question was never posed

01:08:41.010 --> 01:08:42.850
on the world institution,

01:08:42.850 --> 01:08:45.420
since the founding of the
United Nation in 1945.

01:08:45.420 --> 01:08:47.570
The United Nation need to rethink,

01:08:47.570 --> 01:08:50.510
in that rethinking process
we need to consider

01:08:50.510 --> 01:08:52.380
those kinds of state sovereignty.

01:08:52.380 --> 01:08:55.610
All of the (indistinct),
just war, intervention.

01:08:55.610 --> 01:08:58.610
Chapter six and seven are
laid out for a reason,

01:08:58.610 --> 01:08:59.443
we know that.

01:08:59.443 --> 01:09:01.010
UN charter, chapter six and seven.

01:09:01.010 --> 01:09:04.170
These are all elements to rethink

01:09:04.170 --> 01:09:06.540
for the international
diplomatic community.

01:09:06.540 --> 01:09:08.300
And all the United State department,

01:09:08.300 --> 01:09:10.670
this as a global affair
that's moving forward

01:09:10.670 --> 01:09:13.030
with some sort of
element that ASEAN leader

01:09:13.030 --> 01:09:14.130
might maybe listen.

01:09:14.130 --> 01:09:17.050
But hopeless, ASEAN is a
very hopeless institution,

01:09:17.050 --> 01:09:20.750
because Malaysia, Singapore and Indonesia

01:09:20.750 --> 01:09:22.790
are three respectable countries,

01:09:22.790 --> 01:09:25.640
in terms of the freedom of individuals.

01:09:25.640 --> 01:09:27.860
The human rights violation and all that.

01:09:27.860 --> 01:09:29.740
Other than that, there are not much.

01:09:29.740 --> 01:09:32.433
So that would be my two cents.

01:09:36.460 --> 01:09:38.350
- We have a couple more minutes left.

01:09:38.350 --> 01:09:40.300
We were planning to end at 1:15,

01:09:40.300 --> 01:09:42.210
we can go for a few minutes beyond that.

01:09:42.210 --> 01:09:44.660
But there's two questions...

01:09:46.160 --> 01:09:48.230
That are a little bit more specific,

01:09:48.230 --> 01:09:50.880
but one of them builds
from the UN discussion

01:09:50.880 --> 01:09:54.530
that we were just talking
about, representation in the UN.

01:09:54.530 --> 01:09:57.000
And there's another
aspect of representation

01:09:57.000 --> 01:10:00.483
about the refugees in Mizoram
that's raised by Zoma.

01:10:02.260 --> 01:10:04.500
And I wondered if you could speak to that,

01:10:04.500 --> 01:10:06.360
but maybe think a little bit more broadly

01:10:06.360 --> 01:10:08.230
about the representation issue.

01:10:08.230 --> 01:10:11.400
And people who are leaving Myanmar

01:10:11.400 --> 01:10:15.340
for various purposes and what
can be done to support them.

01:10:15.340 --> 01:10:17.950
And then, there's another
question after that,

01:10:17.950 --> 01:10:19.250
that I hope we can turn to,

01:10:19.250 --> 01:10:23.180
about speculations on
the military logistics

01:10:23.180 --> 01:10:25.300
of the actual opposition groups.

01:10:25.300 --> 01:10:27.460
Do they have a chance?

01:10:27.460 --> 01:10:29.430
And so I'd like to talk to that.

01:10:29.430 --> 01:10:31.927
And I think we may run
out of time at that point,

01:10:31.927 --> 01:10:33.363
but we'll see where we get.

01:10:35.440 --> 01:10:38.690
David, you haven't spoken
since the last time.

01:10:38.690 --> 01:10:40.660
Do you want to start this one...

01:10:42.540 --> 01:10:45.253
About representation of refugees, perhaps?

01:10:49.450 --> 01:10:51.310
- India is slightly
different from Myanmar,

01:10:51.310 --> 01:10:54.920
because they have the federal rule.

01:10:54.920 --> 01:10:58.260
For example, many Chin
people fled to Mizoram,

01:10:58.260 --> 01:11:01.830
and Mizoram have their own way of

01:11:01.830 --> 01:11:04.250
making the decisions to welcome them.

01:11:04.250 --> 01:11:05.083
That's good news.

01:11:05.083 --> 01:11:07.550
And I would like to express
some of the Myanmar people

01:11:07.550 --> 01:11:08.810
who joined this panel.

01:11:08.810 --> 01:11:10.900
Thank you all for welcoming those,

01:11:10.900 --> 01:11:13.160
especially Chin and Kachin people,

01:11:13.160 --> 01:11:15.803
for welcoming them in your home state.

01:11:16.980 --> 01:11:20.250
I really don't know,
since this has more to do

01:11:20.250 --> 01:11:22.650
with the UN recommendations
of the refugees.

01:11:22.650 --> 01:11:25.780
I really don't know whether
I might have some insight,

01:11:25.780 --> 01:11:27.590
perhaps, I think Scot Marciel

01:11:27.590 --> 01:11:29.710
might have more insight about that.

01:11:29.710 --> 01:11:31.810
- Go ahead Scot, if you'd like to jump in.

01:11:33.030 --> 01:11:35.990
- Okay, I'm certainly not
an expert on this issue,

01:11:35.990 --> 01:11:37.400
but I would like to say two things.

01:11:37.400 --> 01:11:40.580
First, on the UN I know we all,

01:11:40.580 --> 01:11:42.420
we tend to think of the UN as some

01:11:43.500 --> 01:11:45.520
independent or institution.

01:11:45.520 --> 01:11:47.090
And it is in a way,

01:11:47.090 --> 01:11:49.630
you have the Secretary
General and his staff.

01:11:49.630 --> 01:11:51.510
But fundamentally,

01:11:51.510 --> 01:11:54.540
so you have UN organizations

01:11:54.540 --> 01:11:56.470
that work directly for
the Secretary General.

01:11:56.470 --> 01:12:00.060
For example, managing the
refugee issue and so on.

01:12:00.060 --> 01:12:02.750
But when the UN, when you talk
about the General Assembly,

01:12:02.750 --> 01:12:04.520
or the Security Council.

01:12:04.520 --> 01:12:06.460
It's a collection of countries,

01:12:06.460 --> 01:12:09.501
it's not that when the
UN Security Council,

01:12:09.501 --> 01:12:11.940
or General Assembly fails to do something,

01:12:11.940 --> 01:12:13.730
it's not the UN per se.

01:12:13.730 --> 01:12:17.280
It's because a block of countries says no,

01:12:17.280 --> 01:12:20.750
and it's important to keep that in mind.

01:12:20.750 --> 01:12:22.930
On the refugee issue...

01:12:24.490 --> 01:12:27.360
Generally the UN High
Commissioner for refugees

01:12:28.430 --> 01:12:32.460
and his agency will seek access to people

01:12:32.460 --> 01:12:36.340
ho have fled, who are seeking asylum.

01:12:36.340 --> 01:12:38.130
It depends on the host
countries willingness

01:12:38.130 --> 01:12:39.790
to let the UN interview them.

01:12:39.790 --> 01:12:41.640
And then the UN would interview them,

01:12:41.640 --> 01:12:43.100
UN experts would interview them

01:12:43.100 --> 01:12:45.500
and determine whether they have,

01:12:45.500 --> 01:12:47.913
whether they qualify for refugee status.

01:12:51.536 --> 01:12:54.440
To say it's, technical
issue sounds so impersonal,

01:12:54.440 --> 01:12:58.540
but it's the UN does individual
decisions on those refugees

01:12:58.540 --> 01:13:00.960
are based on certain criteria.

01:13:00.960 --> 01:13:05.200
But the key is for the UN
high commissioner for refugees

01:13:05.200 --> 01:13:08.250
to be granted access by
whichever country is hosting,

01:13:08.250 --> 01:13:10.823
in this case, it would
be Thailand and India.

01:13:11.800 --> 01:13:14.690
And so, that's really where that stands.

01:13:14.690 --> 01:13:18.100
And I don't know what
discussions are going on

01:13:18.100 --> 01:13:20.170
between the UN and the
government of India,

01:13:20.170 --> 01:13:21.060
and the government of Thailand.

01:13:21.060 --> 01:13:23.380
I'm sure there are lots
of discussions happening,

01:13:23.380 --> 01:13:24.930
but I'm just not privy to them.

01:13:26.020 --> 01:13:28.280
- Well, as far as I know

01:13:28.280 --> 01:13:31.410
the situation of the refugee status,

01:13:31.410 --> 01:13:35.740
waiting either in India or
Thailand is more or less

01:13:35.740 --> 01:13:38.253
directly related to the
recognition of the NUG.

01:13:40.090 --> 01:13:41.820
They having asked a lot of people

01:13:41.820 --> 01:13:44.000
who are looking for the refugee status,

01:13:44.000 --> 01:13:46.193
they have been asked
whether they supported

01:13:47.567 --> 01:13:49.730
the NUG statement on the September 7th.

01:13:49.730 --> 01:13:54.730
And the interpretation of their
statements from some agency

01:13:55.040 --> 01:13:59.020
is more or less like supporting violence.

01:13:59.020 --> 01:14:01.840
But as far as I understand the statements

01:14:01.840 --> 01:14:05.250
by NUG on the September 7th is

01:14:05.250 --> 01:14:08.520
saying the state of emergency, that's all.

01:14:08.520 --> 01:14:10.940
This is the state of emergency,

01:14:10.940 --> 01:14:14.380
but some of the domestic
and international media

01:14:14.380 --> 01:14:19.380
also interpret that as the
D-Day for the UMP revolution,

01:14:19.980 --> 01:14:20.813
something like that.

01:14:20.813 --> 01:14:25.200
That's why some of the
international agency interpreted,

01:14:25.200 --> 01:14:29.640
and then they asked
the refugee applicants,

01:14:29.640 --> 01:14:33.480
saying that if you support
the statements by NUG

01:14:33.480 --> 01:14:36.057
on the 7th of September,
are you supporting violence?

01:14:36.057 --> 01:14:37.990
Something like that.

01:14:37.990 --> 01:14:41.320
I think the whole ideological conflict

01:14:41.320 --> 01:14:45.040
and understanding about the
struggle of our revolution

01:14:45.040 --> 01:14:47.700
by the international community.

01:14:47.700 --> 01:14:50.790
This is very, pretty much, very important

01:14:50.790 --> 01:14:53.960
and the pretty much impactful.

01:14:53.960 --> 01:14:55.880
That's why these

01:14:55.880 --> 01:14:56.970
counted...

01:14:58.140 --> 01:15:03.140
The interpretation, and the...

01:15:03.370 --> 01:15:07.210
Reflecting on the media not as if

01:15:07.210 --> 01:15:08.250
its

01:15:08.250 --> 01:15:11.170
the original document set.

01:15:11.170 --> 01:15:13.530
So be more...

01:15:14.770 --> 01:15:17.830
Try to dig enough what's really going on,

01:15:17.830 --> 01:15:20.810
and what's the meaning of the statements.

01:15:20.810 --> 01:15:25.010
And the status of the
NUG should be recognized

01:15:25.010 --> 01:15:27.883
not by this statement.

01:15:29.379 --> 01:15:31.433
That's my thought.

01:15:32.790 --> 01:15:34.320
- Thank you.

01:15:34.320 --> 01:15:37.890
We just have two or three more minutes,

01:15:37.890 --> 01:15:39.450
and I'd like to end.

01:15:39.450 --> 01:15:43.570
although it may be a sobering
way to end the conversation,

01:15:43.570 --> 01:15:46.997
but there is this question
from (indistinct).

01:15:48.695 --> 01:15:51.640
About the PDF's relative inexperience

01:15:51.640 --> 01:15:53.493
in military logistics.

01:15:55.530 --> 01:15:58.190
And this concern about its ability

01:15:58.190 --> 01:16:00.463
to prevail over the Tatmadaw.

01:16:01.770 --> 01:16:04.480
I would be interested in hearing this.

01:16:04.480 --> 01:16:06.630
After we speak about this,

01:16:06.630 --> 01:16:10.090
what I will do is then stop the recording

01:16:10.090 --> 01:16:12.070
and we can have an open
conversation for those

01:16:12.070 --> 01:16:14.730
who wish to stick around for
another ten minutes after that.

01:16:14.730 --> 01:16:18.000
but maybe we can make this
the final formal response

01:16:18.000 --> 01:16:19.373
to a panel discussion.

01:16:20.937 --> 01:16:21.770
And...

01:16:23.160 --> 01:16:27.283
Maybe Katun you could
start with your response.

01:16:28.800 --> 01:16:29.650
- Wow (chuckles).

01:16:31.510 --> 01:16:36.510
The UNHC question I would
like to connect to this,

01:16:37.370 --> 01:16:38.863
respond to this question.

01:16:39.920 --> 01:16:41.903
If UNHC are...

01:16:43.076 --> 01:16:45.126
If they can function within (indistinct),

01:16:46.650 --> 01:16:48.430
and working with (indistinct).

01:16:48.430 --> 01:16:51.090
If they cannot send their own personnel's,

01:16:51.090 --> 01:16:53.530
this is a time to actually
to be brave and bold.

01:16:53.530 --> 01:16:56.060
If they want to really
help the situation inside,

01:16:56.060 --> 01:16:58.520
there are internally displaced people.

01:16:58.520 --> 01:17:02.100
As David already said
the city in Chin state

01:17:02.100 --> 01:17:04.530
has only 28 residents left.

01:17:04.530 --> 01:17:07.120
Where did they go, how do we help them?

01:17:07.120 --> 01:17:08.060
Right?

01:17:08.060 --> 01:17:09.410
Of course, to the India.

01:17:09.410 --> 01:17:11.540
And then other area
within Myanmar as well.

01:17:11.540 --> 01:17:12.373
With that,

01:17:13.440 --> 01:17:17.250
also the question of how do we...

01:17:19.400 --> 01:17:20.900
Can you rephrase a
little bit that question?

01:17:20.900 --> 01:17:22.830
I did not read that question Erik,

01:17:22.830 --> 01:17:24.033
if you don't mind.

01:17:25.340 --> 01:17:30.340
- Yeah, the question is basically
does the opposition group

01:17:31.980 --> 01:17:35.450
have a chance of prevailing
over the Tatmadaw.

01:17:35.450 --> 01:17:38.440
It's a military question
in a sense to say,

01:17:38.440 --> 01:17:42.660
if it turns to full violent resistance,

01:17:42.660 --> 01:17:45.080
what are the chances of winning?

01:17:45.080 --> 01:17:50.060
- Thank you, I think
the convention of war,

01:17:50.060 --> 01:17:52.720
they are well-prepared, the
military is well-prepared.

01:17:52.720 --> 01:17:55.777
And what the PDF and others are imagining,

01:17:55.777 --> 01:17:59.770
are a war of attrition
type, attrition war.

01:17:59.770 --> 01:18:02.440
Which is although what broader sense

01:18:02.440 --> 01:18:05.070
of international economic
sanctions, and so on.

01:18:05.070 --> 01:18:09.070
Try to chip away the power of the existing

01:18:09.070 --> 01:18:10.220
authority anti-government.

01:18:10.220 --> 01:18:13.050
These are in line with
that kind of thinking,

01:18:13.050 --> 01:18:16.310
I think if they engage
in such kind of war.

01:18:16.310 --> 01:18:19.540
And at the same time, if they engage with

01:18:19.540 --> 01:18:23.240
some of the low-level
soldiers within the military,

01:18:23.240 --> 01:18:25.550
start up conversation with them.

01:18:25.550 --> 01:18:28.450
And what the Chin, and CNF, and UG,

01:18:28.450 --> 01:18:30.200
has been recently offering them

01:18:30.200 --> 01:18:33.130
some sort of reward;
Financial and safety for them,

01:18:33.130 --> 01:18:37.320
if they want to join the public
and in a peaceful CDM way.

01:18:37.320 --> 01:18:39.070
If they can empty out,

01:18:39.070 --> 01:18:42.300
which is although the
intention of CDM movement,

01:18:42.300 --> 01:18:45.720
the civil servants who wanted
to cripple the function

01:18:45.720 --> 01:18:47.190
of the military council.

01:18:47.190 --> 01:18:48.750
And who want to actually don't see

01:18:48.750 --> 01:18:52.400
that military council's
government properly working

01:18:52.400 --> 01:18:54.870
as an authoritarian government.

01:18:54.870 --> 01:18:59.870
CDM has that intention and so
they can sort of work with PDF

01:18:59.980 --> 01:19:01.560
and the NUG can work with,

01:19:01.560 --> 01:19:03.870
which they are already beginning to.

01:19:03.870 --> 01:19:07.900
If that combined with what PDF are doing,

01:19:07.900 --> 01:19:09.740
I think it is a just war.

01:19:09.740 --> 01:19:12.980
It is just, if you are
taking down the airplanes

01:19:12.980 --> 01:19:16.340
and trucks in Mytel tower.

01:19:16.340 --> 01:19:21.010
Which will be used by the
military to kill its own people.

01:19:21.010 --> 01:19:23.080
They are not attacking people,

01:19:23.080 --> 01:19:25.180
civilian or the military men here,

01:19:25.180 --> 01:19:27.220
they are just basically taking away,

01:19:27.220 --> 01:19:29.900
like Kachin, KIA has started way back.

01:19:29.900 --> 01:19:32.760
In the gasoline truck
coming in from China,

01:19:32.760 --> 01:19:36.220
destroying them on the road,
letting the driver flee.

01:19:36.220 --> 01:19:38.443
All kinds of these
kinds of peaceful action

01:19:38.443 --> 01:19:42.030
that they are doing a type of
war, attrition if you will.

01:19:42.030 --> 01:19:45.640
And that kind of war, and
strategy well-coordinated,

01:19:45.640 --> 01:19:49.830
will be, I think, quite useful
for making the military,

01:19:49.830 --> 01:19:52.340
especially low-level
soldier all the way to maybe

01:19:52.340 --> 01:19:55.290
regional commander level to join the CDM.

01:19:55.290 --> 01:19:58.190
And then empty out the military
institution at the top,

01:19:58.190 --> 01:20:00.730
who will not change
their mind at this point.

01:20:00.730 --> 01:20:03.570
And they have so much
stake in their families,

01:20:03.570 --> 01:20:05.100
like Ma Thida was saying,

01:20:05.100 --> 01:20:07.300
their future, their businesses, and so on.

01:20:07.300 --> 01:20:11.271
If NUG and PDF can orchestrate that,

01:20:11.271 --> 01:20:13.070
and (indistinct) what they were doing.

01:20:13.070 --> 01:20:17.760
So what I'm saying is there
a broader type of activity

01:20:18.760 --> 01:20:22.027
is needed to really win this war.

01:20:22.027 --> 01:20:24.810
And that of course need to be detail out.

01:20:24.810 --> 01:20:26.620
So for instance, military soldier

01:20:26.620 --> 01:20:28.660
who are ordered to shoot on the street.

01:20:28.660 --> 01:20:30.520
They can point it into the round duration,

01:20:30.520 --> 01:20:31.710
and instead of shooting people,

01:20:31.710 --> 01:20:33.297
they can shoot it to other people.

01:20:33.297 --> 01:20:36.350
And so that kind of military man's,

01:20:36.350 --> 01:20:38.400
their own internal resistant

01:20:38.400 --> 01:20:39.980
against their own leaders order.

01:20:39.980 --> 01:20:43.050
Making sure that their trucks,
the wire is not working,

01:20:43.050 --> 01:20:45.430
the battery is not
charged, and the gasoline

01:20:45.430 --> 01:20:49.110
is not enough to arrive
from point A to point B.

01:20:49.110 --> 01:20:52.120
Military men if they wanted to join CDM

01:20:52.120 --> 01:20:55.300
in such a way from inside
without taking off uniform,

01:20:55.300 --> 01:20:56.470
and they can do so.

01:20:56.470 --> 01:20:59.410
And these kinds of
mechanism can be implemented

01:20:59.410 --> 01:21:02.250
with the coordination
of NUG PDF strategies,

01:21:02.250 --> 01:21:04.880
and communication with these potential CDM

01:21:05.960 --> 01:21:07.470
thinking military men.

01:21:07.470 --> 01:21:09.000
If that kind of war,

01:21:09.000 --> 01:21:10.740
if that kind of strategy
can be structured,

01:21:10.740 --> 01:21:13.260
I think there's a chance of winning.

01:21:13.260 --> 01:21:15.860
If you are going out to conventional war,

01:21:15.860 --> 01:21:17.290
who know?

01:21:17.290 --> 01:21:20.370
A flight from China with military
men on the side may come,

01:21:20.370 --> 01:21:24.020
that's a very sobering
international relation,

01:21:24.020 --> 01:21:27.160
security imagination I'm thinking here.

01:21:27.160 --> 01:21:29.540
I don't mean to say it could
happen or it will happen,

01:21:29.540 --> 01:21:32.260
but it is possibility there, right?

01:21:32.260 --> 01:21:35.360
So all the way to the support from China,

01:21:35.360 --> 01:21:36.933
and possibly the Russian military,

01:21:36.933 --> 01:21:39.550
then maybe some Israeli
communication equipment

01:21:39.550 --> 01:21:42.470
that are making money out
of this kind of a crisis

01:21:42.470 --> 01:21:43.840
in the world for a long time.

01:21:43.840 --> 01:21:46.150
These kinds of things had
to be really orchestrated

01:21:46.150 --> 01:21:49.400
in thinking process and
structuring the war that

01:21:49.400 --> 01:21:51.930
NUG might be intending to do.

01:21:51.930 --> 01:21:54.410
I do not know exactly
what they are thinking.

01:21:54.410 --> 01:21:56.633
That would be where I would leave.

01:21:58.570 --> 01:21:59.530
- Thank you.

01:21:59.530 --> 01:22:02.090
If anyone has a short final comment,

01:22:02.090 --> 01:22:03.050
I'd love to hear that.

01:22:03.050 --> 01:22:04.660
And then I'll bring it to a close,

01:22:04.660 --> 01:22:07.310
and then we'll have an
informal discussion afterward.

01:22:09.180 --> 01:22:10.483
Any final comments?

01:22:11.600 --> 01:22:14.140
- Well, I think the formal intention

01:22:14.140 --> 01:22:18.540
of this armed resistance is...

01:22:18.540 --> 01:22:23.480
As the military have only
the language of weapons,

01:22:23.480 --> 01:22:25.280
they have no other language.

01:22:25.280 --> 01:22:29.880
For that reasons, the revolutions...

01:22:29.880 --> 01:22:32.850
Groups, decided to make sure

01:22:32.850 --> 01:22:36.440
the military started listening to them

01:22:36.440 --> 01:22:37.880
with this arms struggle.

01:22:37.880 --> 01:22:41.210
And the final position
will be on the table

01:22:41.210 --> 01:22:42.460
by the (indistinct) leaders.

01:22:42.460 --> 01:22:47.330
That's the real intention
from the very beginning

01:22:47.330 --> 01:22:49.463
for the UMP revolution, I think.

01:22:52.150 --> 01:22:54.310
